================================================================================
AUTOMATED CODE SYNTHESIS & AI REIMPLEMENTATION COVENANT
================================================================================

1. Purpose and Intent:
   This covenant establishes binding restrictions on the automated, machine-
   assisted, or artificial-intelligence-driven harvesting, decompilation,
   translation, synthesis, or reimplementation of this software's proprietary
   algorithms, zero-allocation data structures, queue-reactive models, and
   matching engine architectures for commercial exploitation.

2. Commercial AI Synthesis Restriction:
   You may NOT input, prompt, fine-tune, ingest, embed, or process this source
   code, its architecture specifications, algorithmic structures, or non-public
   benchmarks into any generative artificial intelligence system, large language
   model (LLM), neural code translation engine, or automated code synthesis tool
   for the purpose of generating, deriving, or outputting a commercial derivative
   work, clean-room commercial reimplementation, or functional clone in any
   programming language (including C++, Rust, C, Java, Go, Zig, or Python)
   without an explicit, executed commercial license from the copyright holder.

3. Contractual Enforceability and Derivative Work Definition:
   Under state and federal contract law, the copyright regimes of Berne
   Convention signatory nations, and the Trade Secrets framework:
   (a) Any functional reproduction or semantic translation produced by an AI
       or LLM that reproduces the algorithmic structures, sequence-form
       microstructure dynamics, zero-tombstone slotmap unlinking, or state-
       dependent intensity formulas of this software shall be deemed a
       derivative work governed by this license.
   (b) Using this software to prompt or instruct an AI model to produce
       unlicensed commercial software constitutes a direct breach of this
       license agreement and intentional interference with intellectual
       property rights.

4. Academic and Open Research Use:
   Academic analysis, non-commercial peer-reviewed research, educational study,
   and open scientific citation of this codebase by researchers and non-profit
   academic institutions are expressly permitted under Section 1, provided
   source attribution is preserved.

5. Commercial Licensing Inquiries:
   For commercial licensing, enterprise deployment rights, algorithmic trading
   integration, or proprietary use exemptions, contact the author:
   Radu Irbe (license inquiries: r-irbe on GitHub).
